{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ויקח קרח", :translit "vayikach korach", :gloss "And Korach took"} {:he "סמך מחלוקת לפרשת ציצית", :translit "samach machloket le'parshat tzitzit", :gloss "juxtaposed the dispute to the section of tzitzit"} {:he "שעל ענין ציצית חלק על משה", :translit "she'al inyan tzitzit chalak al moshe", :gloss "for on account of the matter of tzitzit he disputed with Moses"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Juxtaposition (semikhut) of parashiyot: the rebellion narrative follows the tzitzit section at Numbers 15:37–41, motivating a causal link."}], :frame {:text "The Torah places the section of tzitzit (Numbers 15:37–41) immediately before the Korach narrative (Numbers 16:1), and the Ba'al HaTurim reads this juxtaposition as causally significant. A midrashic tradition records that Korach challenged Moses by fashioning garments entirely of tekhelet and asking whether they require tzitzit, mocking the commandment as described in Numbers 15:39.", :sources ["Midrash Tanchuma Korach 2" "Numbers Rabbah 18:3"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ויקח קרח", :translit "vayikach korach", :gloss "And Korach took"} {:he "במקח רע", :translit "bimkach ra", :gloss "a bad purchase"} {:he "עושר שמור לבעליו לרעתו", :translit "oshar shamur le'be'alav l'ra'ato", :gloss "wealth preserved for its owner to his harm"} {:he "עשרו של קרח לרעתו היה לו", :translit "osaro shel korach l'ra'ato hayah lo", :gloss "the wealth of Korach was to his harm"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "ויקח קרח", :b "במקח רע"} {:kind :gematria, :a "עושר שמור לבעליו לרעתו", :b "עשרו של קרח לרעתו"}], :frame {:text "Korach was exceptionally wealthy. The Mishnah at Shabbat 25b identifies wealth among the things that require protection. The psalmist states that treasure is of no benefit to the wicked (Proverbs 10:2). Josephus records that Korach's faction possessed great riches that were swallowed up with them.", :sources ["Shabbat 25b" "Proverbs 10:2" "Josephus Antiquities 4:14"]}}], :arithme